---
/*
 * TEMPLATE - adapt to your product and processors, and have it reviewed by a
 * lawyer before launch. Company details come from src/config.ts. Keep the
 * Danish version (PrivacyDa.astro) in step.
 */
import { SITE, appUrl } from '../../config'
import { path } from '../../i18n/routes'

const e = SITE.legalEntity
---

<p>
  This Privacy Policy describes how {SITE.name} ("we", "us", "our") collects, uses, and protects your
  personal data when you visit our website or use our services ("Service"). We process personal data
  in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and applicable Danish data protection law.
</p>

<h2>Data Controller</h2>
<p>
  The data controller responsible for your personal data is:<br />
  <strong>{e.name}</strong><br />
  {e.registrationLabel}: {e.registrationNumber}<br />
  {e.address}<br />
  Email: {SITE.supportEmail}
</p>

<h2>Data We Collect</h2>
<p>We may collect the following types of information:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Personal data</strong> - your name, email address and billing information.</li>
  <li>
    <strong>Customer data</strong> - data you or your users input into the system as part of using
    the Service, stored and processed only to provide the Service and related services to you.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Usage data</strong> - information about how you interact with the Service, such as log
    files, IP addresses, browser types, device information, and pages visited.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Enquiries</strong> - the name, email address and message you send us through the contact
    form or waitlist on this website.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Controller and Processor Roles</h2>
<p>
  For personal data about third parties that you or your users store in the Service, you are the data
  controller and we act as your data processor. That processing is governed by the Data Processing
  section of our <a href={path('terms', 'en')}>Terms of Service</a>. For account, billing, usage and
  enquiry data we are the data controller.
</p>

<h2>Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Performance of a contract</strong> (Art. 6(1)(b)) - account data and usage data are
    processed to deliver the service you have subscribed to.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Legal obligation</strong> (Art. 6(1)(c)) - billing records are retained to comply with
    Danish bookkeeping law (bogføringsloven).
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Legitimate interest</strong> (Art. 6(1)(f)) - transactional emails (password reset,
    notifications), service-related communications, replies to your enquiries, and in-app support chat
    are based on our legitimate interest in operating and supporting the service.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Data Processors and Third-Party Services</h2>
<p>
  We share personal data only with processors necessary to deliver the service. All processors are
  bound by data processing agreements (DPAs) in accordance with Art. 28 GDPR:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Stripe</strong> - payment processing. Receives billing contact information and processes
    card data on our behalf. EU customers are served by Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd. (Ireland).
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Hetzner Online GmbH</strong> - cloud infrastructure and hosting. Stores and processes data
    on servers located in the EU on our behalf.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Transactional email provider</strong> - delivery of system emails. Receives your email
    address and the content of system notifications. The provider is located outside the EU/EEA; see
    International Data Transfers below.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>tawk.to inc.</strong> - live chat support inside the signed-in application. Receives the
    messages you send and technical data required to operate the chat session.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell or share your personal data with third parties for marketing purposes.</p>

<h2>International Data Transfers</h2>
<p>
  Some of our processors transfer personal data outside the EU/EEA. Transfers to Stripe's US entities
  are safeguarded by the EU-US Data Privacy Framework and Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) approved
  by the European Commission. Transfers to our transactional email provider and to tawk.to (US) are
  safeguarded by Standard Contractual Clauses. In all cases an adequate level of protection for your
  data is ensured.
</p>

<h2>Cookies, Analytics, and Chat</h2>
<p>
  This website sets no cookies. For web statistics we use a self-hosted, cookieless analytics tool
  running on our own EU-hosted infrastructure. It stores nothing on your device, collects only
  aggregated usage statistics, and shares no data with third parties.
</p>
<p>
  The signed-in application uses a session cookie strictly necessary for authentication, and offers a
  live support chat (Tawk.to), which sets cookies required to operate the chat session. We do not use
  advertising or third-party tracking cookies.
</p>

<h2>Data Retention</h2>
<p>
  Account and usage data is retained for as long as your account is active. Audit logs, including IP
  addresses, are kept while your account is active and are included in your data export. When an
  account is deleted it is permanently purged, including audit logs, after a 30-day grace period.
  Billing records are retained for 5 years from the end of the financial year they concern, to comply
  with Danish bookkeeping requirements. Enquiries are kept only as long as needed to handle them.
</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>
  We protect personal data with appropriate technical and organisational measures (Art. 32 GDPR),
  including encryption in transit (TLS), role-based access controls, and hosting on EU-located
  infrastructure.
</p>

<h2>Automated Decision-Making</h2>
<p>
  We do not use your personal data for automated decision-making or profiling within the meaning of
  Art. 22 GDPR.
</p>

<h2>Your Rights</h2>
<p>Under GDPR you have the right to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
  <li>Rectify inaccurate data</li>
  <li>Erase your data ("right to be forgotten")</li>
  <li>Export your data in a portable format</li>
  <li>Object to or restrict certain processing activities</li>
  <li>
    Lodge a complaint with the Danish Data Protection Agency (Datatilsynet), <a
      href="https://www.datatilsynet.dk"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">www.datatilsynet.dk</a
    >
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  You can exercise these rights from your account settings under <a
    href={appUrl('/settings/privacy')}>Privacy &amp; Data</a
  >, or by contacting us at {SITE.supportEmail}.
</p>

<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>
  We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be announced by email and
  reflected in the "Last updated" date at the top of this page.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>For privacy-related inquiries please contact us at {SITE.supportEmail}.</p>
